<script>
  // Fields as declared in packages/basecamp/db/schema.lite. A `{` in markup
  // opens an expression, so the sample lives here and is printed as text.
  const DECLARED = `model Monitor {
  name                 String  @trim @length(1, 200)
  url                  String  @trim @url
  method               HttpMethod @default(GET)
  intervalSeconds      Int     @default(120)   @gte(60) @lte(86400)
  retries              Int     @default(2)     @gte(0) @lte(10)
  retryIntervalSeconds Int     @default(120)   @gte(60)
  timeoutMs            Int     @default(10000) @gte(1000) @lte(60000)
  acceptedStatus       String  @default("200-299") @trim @length(3, 200)
  isInverted           Boolean @default(false)
  resendEvery          Int     @default(0)     @gte(0)
  // …
}

model AlertRule {
  name         String   @trim @length(1, 200)
  severity     AlertSeverity @default(warning)
  metricName   String   @trim @length(1, 200)
  operator     ComparisonOp  @default(gt)
  threshold    Float
  forMinutes   Int      @default(0) @gte(0) @lte(1440)
  isActive     Boolean  @default(true)
  snoozedUntil DateTime? @system
  // …
}`
</script>

<section id="watch" class="bc-section">
  <div class="container stack">
    <p class="eyebrow">Monitoring and alerting</p>
    <h2>Hear it from Basecamp, not from a customer.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Basecamp asks your URLs whether they are up, notices when a box stops
      checking in, and grades the numbers you set rules on. When something
      changes, the right person hears about it once, on the channel they chose.
    </p>

    <div class="bc-split">
      <ul class="bc-points">
        <li>
          <strong>Probes from outside, tolerant of a blip.</strong>
          A monitor is a URL, a method and the status codes that count
          (<code>200-299,301</code> by default), checked every two minutes from
          the Basecamp process. It goes down only after its retries fail in a row,
          so one 502 behind a load balancer pages nobody, and a monitor can
          re-page every N checks while it stays down.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Alert rules fire on a breach that holds, and clear on a real reading.</strong>
          A rule names a metric, an operator, a threshold and how many minutes the
          breach must last. It is checked every minute against minute-level
          readings, and a metric that stops arriving never resolves an open alert
          or fires a new one. Snooze a rule for a maintenance window, up to a
          week, and it wakes by itself.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A quiet box and a failed job both get noticed.</strong>
          Outposts check in every 30 seconds by default. Past the grace you set
          (two minutes unless you change it) the server is marked unreachable
          and its workspace is told. A scheduled job keeps its cron
          schedule, records every run with output, retries, and tells your
          workspace when the last attempt fails.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pagers and people are separate.</strong>
          A rule or monitor delivers to the channels you attach: Slack, PagerDuty,
          email, a webhook, or another FrontierJS app's chat. Each member also gets
          in-app notices, email where a mailer is configured, and a phone ping
          for the failures. Each person sets their own in-app and email
          preferences per kind of notice.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="bc-proof">
        <pre class="code">{DECLARED}</pre>
        <figcaption>
          Fields excerpted from <code>packages/basecamp/db/schema.lite</code>, models
          <code>Monitor</code> and <code>AlertRule</code> (comments and relations
          trimmed). Grading is <code>domain/monitor/probe.ts</code> and
          <code>jobs/alert-evaluate.job.ts</code>.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p class="bc-more">
      Read more:
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/basecamp/docs/layout.md">Basecamp layout</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/basecamp/jobs.snapshot.md">every job and its schedule</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/basecamp/notifications.snapshot.md">every notification and its transports</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/outpost/README.md">Outpost and its heartbeat</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
